@startuml SD_MonitorHubNetwork
title UC-F01 - Monitor the Mobility Hub Network
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Operator
boundary "Operator Dashboard" as UI
control "FleetDashboardController" as C
entity "HubRepository" as H
entity "VehicleRepository" as V
entity "IncidentRepository" as I
entity "Status/Freshness Store" as S

Operator -> UI: Open Network Map
UI -> C: getNetworkOverview(operatorSession)
alt Operator is not authorized
  C --> UI: Access denied
  UI --> Operator: Show authorization error
else Operator is authorized
  C -> H: listHubsWithCapacity()
  H --> C: Hubs and parking capacity
  C -> V: listVehiclesByHubAndStatus()
  V --> C: Distribution, availability, battery
  C -> I: listOpenIncidents()
  I --> C: Open incidents
  C -> S: getChargingStatusAndFreshness()
  S --> C: Charging status and timestamps
  alt Required data cannot be retrieved
    C --> UI: Partial/unavailable data with source timestamps
    UI --> Operator: Mark affected cards unavailable
  else Required data is available
    loop For each Hub
      C -> C: Calculate occupancy and resource shortage
      C -> C: Mark stale observations (FR-NI-03)
    end
    opt Hub shortage or capacity risk (FR-NI-06)
      C -> C: Attach existing alert/recommendation
    end
    C --> UI: Overview, KPIs, alerts, freshness
    UI --> Operator: Show dashboard and Network Map
  end
end
note over C,S
Read-only use case. Alerts can come from background rules;
opening the dashboard does not create an assignment.
end note
@enduml
